<title>USA: U.S. Feb housing starts rose 12.2 percent.</title>
<headline>U.S. Feb housing starts rose 12.2 percent.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commerce housing starts and</p>
<p>building permits, seasonally adjusted annual rates, in 1,000s:</p>
<p> PCT CHANGE: Feb     Jan (Prev)     Dec (Prev)   Feb97/96</p>
<p> -Starts    12.2     0.7    2.0    -9.0  -11.0	  0.5</p>
<p> -Permits    3.0    -1.5   -1.9     0.3    0.3	  1.8</p>
<p> RATES	 Feb     Jan (Prev)     Dec (Prev)   Feb 1996</p>
<p> -Starts   1,528   1,362  1,350   1,353  1,323	1,520</p>
<p> -Permits  1,442   1,400  1,395   1,422  1,422	1,417</p>
<p> STARTS:     Feb     Jan (Prev)     Dec (Prev)   Feb 1996</p>
<p> -Single   1,215   1,117  1,108   1,024  1,005	1,188</p>
<p> -Multiple   313     245    242     329    318	  332</p>
<p> PERMITS     Feb     Jan (Prev)     Dec (Prev)   Feb 1996</p>
<p> -Single   1,075   1,051  1,054   1,015  1,015	1,087</p>
<p> -Multiple   367     349    341     407    407	  330</p>
<p> FEB STARTS--Pct--Rate    FEB PERMITS--Pct---Rate--------</p>
<p> -N.East   -26.9   128    -Northeast   8.8   160</p>
<p> -Midwest   51.6   385    -Midwest     5.0   314</p>
<p> -South     10.9   661    -South	 1.3   608</p>
<p> -West	 5.0   354    -West	  1.7   360</p>
<p>Actual Starts and Permits, unadjusted in 1,000s:</p>
<p>    -	  Feb     Jan (Prev)     Dec (Prev)   Feb 1996</p>
<p>  Starts	93	81     81	93     91	   96</p>
<p>  Permits     93	89     88     100    100	   95</p>
<p>Wall Street economists had forecast February starts at a 1.45 million unit annual rate.</p>
<p>February starts of single-family homes were up 8.8 percent from January, and multiple-unit starts increased 27.8 percent. February permits for single-family units rose 2.3 percent, while permits for multiple unit dwelling were up 5.2 percent.  </p>
<p>The department said February starts were the highest since March 1994 when they were 1,564,000. The rate of increase in February was the largest since a 13.1 percent gain in July 1995.</p>
<p>The 26.9 percent drop in starts in the Northeast during February was the biggest for that region since a 37.8 percent decrease in December 1990.</p>
